{"name":"Heartless","hex":"#623b70","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heartless","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without feeling, emotion, or concern for others; uncaring; cruel. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Without a physical heart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heartless"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heartless (Carriger novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Heartless is a steampunk paranormal romance novel by Gail Carriger. Released on June 28, 2011, by Orbit Books, Heartless is the fourth book in the New York Times best-selling \"The Parasol Protectorate\" series, each featuring Alexia Tarabotti, a woman without a soul, as its lead character."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/Gail_Carriger_-_Heartless_book_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartless_(Carriger_novel)","wikidata":"Q5692910"},{"title":"Heartless (Kanye West song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Heartless\" is a song by American rapper Kanye West from his fourth studio album, 808s & Heartbreak (2008). The song was written by West, No I.D., Kid Cudi, and Malik Yusef, while being produced by the former two. It was passed on to West during recording sessions, after originally being intended for inclusion on Jay-Z's eleventh studio album, The Blueprint 3 (2009). Following the song's debut at the 2008 Democratic National Convention (DNC), West shared an unmastered version via his blog on October 15, 2008. The song was later serviced to American rhythmic contemporary radio stations as the second single from 808s & Heartbreak on October 28, through Roc-A-Fella and Def Jam. A pop ballad with influences of hip hop and R&B, it features synthesizers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kanyewestheartless.png/330px-Kanyewestheartless.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartless_(Kanye_West_song)","wikidata":"Q2075331"},{"title":"Heartless (2014 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Heartless is a 2014 Indian Hindi-language medical thriller film directed by Shekhar Suman. Shekhar Suman also stars in the film along with his son Adhyayan Suman. The film also features Ariana Ayam, Deepti Naval, Om Puri and Madan Jain amongst others. It released on 7 February 2014, to mixed reviews from critics. The film focuses on anaesthesia awareness, where a patient cannot move or communicate, but is aware to varying degrees of what is happening during surgical procedures. Several critics have noticed striking similarities between the film and the 2007 Hollywood medical thriller Awake, leading some to describe Heartless a copy of said film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Heartless_2014%2C_official_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartless_(2014_film)","wikidata":"Q15715166"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/Gail_Carriger_-_Heartless_book_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/Gail_Carriger_-_Heartless_book_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGail_Carriger_-_Heartless_book_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kanyewestheartless.png/500px-Kanyewestheartless.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kanyewestheartless.png/500px-Kanyewestheartless.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKanyewestheartless.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg/500px-Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg/1280px-Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg/500px-Kanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"West and No I.D. (pictured center and left, respectively) working on the song in Glenwood Studios, Burbank, California.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKanye_West_in_the_Studio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg/500px-Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg/1280px-Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg/500px-Kanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The song gave West his third top five entry of 2008 on the US Billboard Hot 100 in November, while it became his second highest-charting single overall on the Hot 100 two months later.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKanye_West_Shankbone_2009_Vanity_Fair.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Obama_portrait_crop.jpg/500px-Obama_portrait_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Obama_por